UNNECESSARY RE-RENDERS — the main culprit:
Every parent re-render re-renders all children unless you memoize.

React.memo — skip re-render if props unchanged:
const ExpensiveList = React.memo(({ items }) => (
 <ul>{items.map(item => <li key={item.id}>{item.name}</li>)}</ul>
));
// Will only re-render if items reference changes

useMemo — memoize expensive computed values:
const sortedUsers = useMemo(
 () => users.filter(u => u.active).sort((a,b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name)),
 [users] // only recomputes when users changes
);

useCallback — memoize functions (prevents child re-renders):
const handleDelete = useCallback((id: string) => {
 setUsers(prev => prev.filter(u => u.id !== id));
}, []); // stable reference — child with this prop won''t re-render unnecessarily

