WEBASSEMBLY — near-native performance in the browser.

WHAT IS WASM:
Binary instruction format for stack-based virtual machine.
Runs in browser at near-native speed. Not JavaScript.
Use for: computationally intensive code (image processing, cryptography, games, codecs).
Source languages: C, C++, Rust, Go, AssemblyScript.

